%[text] # **RHIT Mass Calibration**
%[text] **Voltage and 2D bowl correction with interactive Z-range, fiducial ROI, peak picker, and iterative refinement**
%[text] This workflow mirrors the standard IVAS calibration steps but in a scriptable form. It calibrates the mass-to-charge axis of a Cameca LEAP RHIT file from the spectrum the file already carries (`pMass`). No EPOS, IVAS reconstruction, or external training data needed. Each section is self-contained and can be re-run independently after the previous sections have been executed.
%[text] 
%[text] ### Pipeline (mirrors IVAS)
%[text] 1. Load the RHIT.
%[text] 2. **Z selection** — pick the voltage range of valid data on the V(z) curve.
%[text] 3. **XY fiducial** — pick the usable detector area on the hit-density map.
%[text] 4. **Peak inspection** — auto-detect peaks in `pMass`, mark spurious ones to exclude.
%[text] 5. **Calibrate** — fit `mc = C(x, y) · VDC · (tof − t_offset)²` on the filtered subset.
%[text] 6. **Iterate** — refine until the mass-resolving power converges.
%[text] 7. Save. \
%[text] 
%[text] *Author*: Prof. Peter Felfer Group @FAU Erlangen-Nürnberg
%%
%[text] ## 1. Setup and dependencies
%[text] *setupToolbox* adds toolbox paths (including `RHIT_imports`). `rhitLoad` calls a Python helper, so Python 3 with `uproot`, `h5py`, `numpy` must be installed (one-time terminal command: `pip3 install uproot h5py numpy`).
setupToolbox; %[output:1a7ce78a]
[s, out] = system('python3 -c "import uproot,h5py,numpy; print(uproot.__version__)"');
if s ~= 0
    error('Python 3 + uproot/h5py/numpy not available.\nRun: pip3 install uproot h5py numpy');
end
fprintf('Python OK; uproot %s\n', strtrim(out)); %[output:31fc6e70]
  %[control:button:0a01]{"position":[1,2]}
%%
%[text] ## 2. Load RHIT
%[text] *rhitLoad* with no arguments opens a file dialog. Returns the per-event *hits* table, embedded Cameca *histograms* (including `pMass`), and instrument *metadata*.
[hits, hist, meta] = rhitLoad; %[output:566b6edf]
fprintf('RHIT events: %d  |  IVAS %s  |  flight path %.1f mm  |  t0 %.2f ns\n', ... %[output:group:6624f720] %[output:3c9d015a]
    height(hits), meta.instrumentParams.ivas_version, ... %[output:3c9d015a]
    meta.instrumentParams.flight_path_mm, meta.instrumentParams.t0_ns); %[output:group:6624f720] %[output:3c9d015a]
  %[control:button:0a02]{"position":[1,2]}
%%
%[text] ## 3. Z selection — pick voltage range from V(z)
%[text] Drag a rectangle on the V(z) curve to select the steady-state region. **Excluded regions:** initial standby, cap material, post-microfracture noise. Double-click inside the rectangle to confirm.
%[text] Sets `vdcMin` and `vdcMax` --- ions outside this range will not be used for the calibration fit (but still get the calibration applied).
fig = figure('Color', 'w', 'Position', [80 80 1100 380]); %[output:6dae57d5]
plot(hits.VDC, '-', 'Color', [0.2 0.4 0.8], 'LineWidth', 0.5); %[output:6dae57d5]
xlabel('ion sequence number'); ylabel('V_{DC} (V)'); grid on; %[output:6dae57d5]
title('Drag a rectangle to select the Z-range, then double-click to confirm'); %[output:6dae57d5]
roiZ = drawrectangle('Color', 'r', 'LineWidth', 1.5, ... %[output:group:064ffbe8] %[output:6dae57d5]
    'Label', 'Z range', 'LabelAlpha', 0.6); %[output:group:064ffbe8] %[output:6dae57d5]
wait(roiZ);
yL = roiZ.Position(2);
yH = yL + roiZ.Position(4);
vdcMin = max(yL, min(hits.VDC));
vdcMax = min(yH, max(hits.VDC));
fprintf('Z range: VDC %.0f V  to  %.0f V  (%.1f%% of ions)\n', ... %[output:group:9372abc7] %[output:8ab65c92]
    vdcMin, vdcMax, 100 * mean(hits.VDC >= vdcMin & hits.VDC <= vdcMax)); %[output:group:9372abc7] %[output:8ab65c92]
  %[control:button:0a03]{"position":[1,2]}
%%
%[text] ## 4. XY fiducial — pick the usable detector area
%[text] Draw an ellipse on the detector hit-density map. **Excluded regions:** the outer rim ("mouse bites"), low-efficiency edges, dead spots. Double-click inside to confirm. The default ellipse covers ~95 % of hits, like IVAS's default.
fig2 = figure('Color', 'w', 'Position', [80 80 700 700]); %[output:4059f8b3]
binX = linspace(-20, 20, 201); binY = binX;
H = histcounts2(hits.detx, hits.dety, binX, binY);
imagesc(binX(1:end-1), binY(1:end-1), log10(H' + 1)); %[output:4059f8b3]
axis image; set(gca, 'YDir', 'normal'); colormap(gca, 'parula'); %[output:4059f8b3]
xlabel('detector x (mm)'); ylabel('detector y (mm)'); %[output:4059f8b3]
title('Drag an ellipse for the XY fiducial, then double-click to confirm'); %[output:4059f8b3]

% Default ellipse: 95th percentile radius
r95 = prctile(sqrt(hits.detx.^2 + hits.dety.^2), 95);
roiDet = drawellipse('Center', [0, 0], 'SemiAxes', [r95, r95], ... %[output:4059f8b3]
    'Color', 'r', 'LineWidth', 1.5, ... %[output:4059f8b3]
    'Label', 'fiducial', 'LabelAlpha', 0.6); %[output:4059f8b3]
wait(roiDet); %[output:4059f8b3]
detMask = inROI(roiDet, hits.detx, hits.dety);

% --- Confirmation: lock ROI, turn green, update title ---
roiDet.Color = [0.10 0.65 0.20];
roiDet.LineWidth = 2;
roiDet.Label = sprintf('  ACCEPTED  (%.1f%% kept)  ', 100*mean(detMask));
roiDet.LabelAlpha = 0.85;
roiDet.InteractionsAllowed = 'none';
title(sprintf(['\\color[rgb]{0.10,0.65,0.20}\\bf  Fiducial accepted: ' ...
    '%.1f%% of ions kept (%d of %d)'], ...
    100*mean(detMask), sum(detMask), height(hits)));

fprintf('[OK]  Fiducial accepted: keeps %d of %d ions (%.1f%%)\n', ... %[output:group:85e02cb0] %[output:9925b3a6]
    sum(detMask), height(hits), 100 * mean(detMask)); %[output:group:85e02cb0] %[output:9925b3a6]
  %[control:button:0a04]{"position":[1,2]}
%%
%[text] ## 5. Peak inspection — review pMass peaks
%[text] *findpeaks* auto-detects peaks in the embedded `pMass`. They are listed in *peakTable*. **Edit *peakTable.use*** to mark which peaks to keep — set `false` to exclude one — then **re-run this section** to refresh the plot. Kept peaks turn **green**, excluded peaks turn **red and crossed-out**. The calibration cost in section 6 builds a window-mask around each kept peak (±3 widths) and uses *only* those regions for the cross-correlation, so removing a peak literally removes it from the fit.
mcEdges = double(hist.massSpectrum.edges);
mcCentr = mcEdges(1:end-1) + diff(mcEdges)/2;
mcVals  = double(hist.massSpectrum.values);

% Build (or refresh) peakTable.  If it already exists with a 'use'
% column, preserve the user's edits — we only re-detect when missing.
if ~exist('peakTable', 'var') || ~istable(peakTable) ...
        || ~ismember('use', peakTable.Properties.VariableNames)
    [pkVals, pkLocsIdx, pkWidths, pkProm] = findpeaks(log1p(mcVals), ...
        'MinPeakProminence', 0.6, 'MinPeakDistance', 25);
    pkMc = mcCentr(pkLocsIdx);
    binDa = mean(diff(mcEdges));
    peakTable = table(pkMc(:), exp(pkVals(:)) - 1, pkProm(:), ...
        pkWidths(:) * binDa, true(numel(pkMc), 1), ...
        'VariableNames', {'mc', 'height', 'prominence', 'widthDa', 'use'});
end

figure('Color', 'w', 'Position', [80 80 1300 500]); %[output:8a72993a]
semilogy(mcCentr, max(mcVals, 1), 'b-', 'LineWidth', 0.6); %[output:8a72993a]
hold on; %[output:8a72993a]
keep = peakTable.use;
% Kept peaks: green triangles, normal label
if any(keep) %[output:8a72993a]
    stem(peakTable.mc(keep), peakTable.height(keep), 'Color', [0.10 0.65 0.20], ...
        'Marker', 'v', 'MarkerFaceColor', [0.10 0.65 0.20], ...
        'BaseValue', 1, 'LineWidth', 0.6); %[output:8a72993a]
    text(peakTable.mc(keep), peakTable.height(keep) * 1.4, ...
        arrayfun(@(m) sprintf('%.2f', m), peakTable.mc(keep), 'UniformOutput', false), ...
        'FontSize', 7, 'HorizontalAlignment', 'center', 'Color', [0.05 0.40 0.10]); %[output:8a72993a]
end
% Excluded peaks: red dashed, strike-through label
if any(~keep) %[output:8a72993a]
    stem(peakTable.mc(~keep), peakTable.height(~keep), 'Color', [0.85 0.10 0.10], ...
        'Marker', 'x', 'MarkerSize', 8, 'LineStyle', '--', ...
        'BaseValue', 1, 'LineWidth', 0.8); %[output:8a72993a]
    text(peakTable.mc(~keep), peakTable.height(~keep) * 1.4, ...
        arrayfun(@(m) sprintf('\\bf{\\rm %.2f \\bf{\\fontsize{8}\\itexcluded}}', m), ...
            peakTable.mc(~keep), 'UniformOutput', false), ...
        'FontSize', 7, 'HorizontalAlignment', 'center', 'Color', [0.85 0.10 0.10]); %[output:8a72993a]
end
xlim([0 80]); xlabel('mass-to-charge (Da)'); ylabel('counts (pMass)'); %[output:8a72993a]
title(sprintf(['pMass:  \\color[rgb]{0.10,0.65,0.20}\\bf%d kept\\rm  ' ...
    '\\color[rgb]{0.85,0.10,0.10}\\bf%d excluded\\rm  \\color{black}' ...
    '(edit peakTable.use, re-run this section to refresh)'], ...
    sum(keep), sum(~keep))); %[output:8a72993a]
grid on; %[output:8a72993a]

fprintf('[OK]  Peaks accepted: %d of %d (set .use=false to exclude, then re-run section)\n', ...
    sum(keep), height(peakTable));
disp(peakTable); %[output:9b6f8b90]
  %[control:button:0a05]{"position":[1,2]}
%%
%[text] ## 6. Calibrate on the selected subset
%[text] Fit voltage + 2D bowl on **only the ions inside both the Z range and the XY fiducial**. The resulting calibration is then applied to *every* ion in the file.
%[text] *rhitCalibrateFromStoredMass* internal pipeline: 9 × 9 detector cells → per-cell pMass-similarity → 2D *xy* polynomial bowl → cross-correlation `t_offset` refinement → re-fit bowl.
mcHi = 100;          % upper mc limit for spectrum matching (Da) %[control:editfield:0a31]{"position":[8,11]}
binWidth = 0.02;     % working bin width (Da) %[control:editfield:0a32]{"position":[12,16]}
gridN = 9;           % detector divided into gridN x gridN cells %[control:editfield:0a33]{"position":[9,10]}
gridHalf = 16;       % cell grid covers +/- gridHalf mm %[control:editfield:0a34]{"position":[12,14]}
bowlDegree = 4;      % 2D xy polynomial degree (15 terms at deg 4) %[control:editfield:0a35]{"position":[14,15]}
minCellHits = 6000;  % cells with fewer hits are skipped %[control:editfield:0a36]{"position":[15,19]}

mask = detMask & hits.VDC >= vdcMin & hits.VDC <= vdcMax;
fprintf('Calibrating on %d / %d ions (%.1f%%)\n', sum(mask), height(hits), 100*mean(mask)); %[output:31709e2a]
hitsROI = hits(mask, :);

% Build a peak-window-masked reference spectrum from the user-edited
% peakTable: zero out everything outside +/- 3 widths of any kept peak.
peaksKept = peakTable(peakTable.use, :);
peakMask = false(size(mcCentr));
for k = 1:height(peaksKept)
    w = max(peaksKept.widthDa(k), 3*binWidth);
    peakMask = peakMask | abs(mcCentr - peaksKept.mc(k)) < 3*w;
end
maskedSpectrum = mcVals;
maskedSpectrum(~peakMask) = 0;
histMasked = hist;
histMasked.massSpectrum = struct('edges', mcEdges, 'values', maskedSpectrum);
fprintf('Reference spectrum keeps %d peak windows (%.1f%% of mc range)\n', ... %[output:group:478087a4] %[output:3afa9eb7]
    height(peaksKept), 100*mean(peakMask)); %[output:group:478087a4] %[output:3afa9eb7]

[~, calib, diag] = rhitCalibrateFromStoredMass(hitsROI, histMasked, meta, ... %[output:group:1ab63ba3] %[output:1c27b6cd]
    'mcHi',          mcHi, ... %[output:1c27b6cd]
    'binWidth',      binWidth, ... %[output:1c27b6cd]
    'gridN',         gridN, ... %[output:1c27b6cd]
    'gridHalf',      gridHalf, ... %[output:1c27b6cd]
    'bowlDegree',    bowlDegree, ... %[output:1c27b6cd]
    'minCellHits',   minCellHits, ... %[output:1c27b6cd]
    'refineTOffset', true, ... %[output:1c27b6cd]
    'verbose',       true); %[output:group:1ab63ba3] %[output:1c27b6cd]

% Apply the resulting calibration to ALL ions (not just the ROI)
hits = rhitApplyCalibration(hits, calib); %[output:019bc799]

fprintf('\nFit:  cells %d / %d  |  residual %.4f%% of C0  |  t_offset %.3f ns\n', ... %[output:group:3fbe6ee1] %[output:31998425]
    diag.calibration.nCells, gridN^2, calib.fitResidualPctC0, calib.tOffsetNs); %[output:group:3fbe6ee1] %[output:31998425]
  %[control:button:0a06]{"position":[1,2]}
%%
%[text] ## 7. Plot calibrated spectrum vs pMass with peak overlay
%[text] Compares your calibrated *hits.mc* (red) to Cameca's stored *pMass* (blue), with the auto-detected peak positions marked. The grey curve is the raw uncalibrated spectrum (no bowl) for reference.
edges = diag.referenceEdges;
centres = edges(1:end-1) + diff(edges)/2;
hCal = histcounts(hits.mc, edges);
[hRaw, ~, ~] = rhitLoad(meta.fileName); %[output:02f58edf]

figure('Color', 'w', 'Position', [80 80 1300 700]); %[output:1d5f3251]
tiledlayout(2, 1, 'TileSpacing', 'compact'); %[output:1d5f3251]
ax1 = nexttile; %[output:1d5f3251]
semilogy(centres, max(double(diag.referenceValues), 1), 'b-', 'LineWidth', 0.6, ... %[output:1d5f3251]
    'DisplayName', 'Cameca pMass'); %[output:1d5f3251]
hold on; %[output:1d5f3251]
semilogy(centres, max(double(hCal), 1), 'r-', 'LineWidth', 0.6, ... %[output:1d5f3251]
    'DisplayName', 'our calibration'); %[output:1d5f3251]
semilogy(centres, max(double(histcounts(hRaw.mc, edges)), 1), '-', ... %[output:1d5f3251]
    'Color', [0.6 0.6 0.6], 'LineWidth', 0.6, 'DisplayName', 'raw rhitLoad'); %[output:1d5f3251]
xline(pkMc, ':', 'Color', [0.4 0.4 0.4]); %[output:1d5f3251]
xlim([0 80]); ylabel('counts'); legend('show'); grid on; %[output:854b2d5a] %[output:1d5f3251]
title('Full spectrum overlay (dotted lines = pMass peaks)'); %[output:1d5f3251]

nexttile; %[output:1d5f3251]
semilogy(centres, max(double(diag.referenceValues), 1), 'b-', 'LineWidth', 0.6); %[output:1d5f3251]
hold on; %[output:1d5f3251]
semilogy(centres, max(double(hCal), 1), 'r-', 'LineWidth', 0.6); %[output:1d5f3251]
xline(pkMc, ':', 'Color', [0.4 0.4 0.4]); %[output:1d5f3251]
xlim([10 35]); xlabel('mass-to-charge (Da)'); ylabel('counts'); grid on; %[output:1d5f3251]
title('Zoom 10 – 35 Da'); %[output:1d5f3251]
  %[control:button:0a07]{"position":[1,2]}
%%
%[text] ## 8. Iterative refinement
%[text] **Mirrors IVAS's voltage ↔ bowl iteration** until mass-resolving power stops improving. At each iteration the previous calibration's `hits.mc` is used as the reference spectrum (instead of pMass), so the calibration converges to a self-consistent state. M/ΔM is computed at the strongest peak in the user-selected mc window below.
%[text] Stops when M/ΔM gain is \< `tolerance` for two iterations in a row, or after `maxIter` iterations.
maxIter = 4; %[control:editfield:0a51]{"position":[11,12]}
tolerance = 0.01; %[control:editfield:0a52]{"position":[13,17]}
peakMcWindow = [26.7 27.3]; % FWHM measured on the strongest peak in this window (Da) %[control:editfield:0a53]{"position":[16,28]}

% M/dM at the strongest peak in peakMcWindow, computed inline
edgesM = peakMcWindow(1):0.005:peakMcWindow(2);
centresM = edgesM(1:end-1) + 0.0025;
hM0 = histcounts(hits.mc, edgesM);
[pkM, ipM] = max(hM0);
halfM = pkM / 2;
LM = find(hM0(1:ipM) < halfM, 1, 'last');
RM = ipM + find(hM0(ipM:end) < halfM, 1, 'first') - 1;
mrp0 = NaN;
if pkM > 20 && ~isempty(LM) && ~isempty(RM)
    mrp0 = centresM(ipM) / max(centresM(RM) - centresM(LM), eps);
end
mrpHistory = NaN(maxIter + 1, 1);
mrpHistory(1) = mrp0;
fprintf('Iter 0 (initial):  M/dM = %.1f\n', mrpHistory(1)); %[output:584dc79f]

bestHits = hits; bestCalib = calib; nNoGain = 0;
for it = 1:maxIter %[output:group:84e2e903]
    edgesIt = 0:binWidth:mcHi;
    refValsIt = histcounts(hits.mc, edgesIt);
    histIt = hist;
    histIt.massSpectrum = struct('edges', edgesIt, 'values', refValsIt);
    [~, calibIt, diagIt] = rhitCalibrateFromStoredMass(hitsROI, histIt, meta, ... %[output:39d7db33] %[output:5f69987c] %[output:8febe17d] %[output:379ba1e6]
        'mcHi', mcHi, 'binWidth', binWidth, ... %[output:39d7db33] %[output:5f69987c] %[output:8febe17d] %[output:379ba1e6]
        'gridN', gridN, 'gridHalf', gridHalf, ... %[output:39d7db33] %[output:5f69987c] %[output:8febe17d] %[output:379ba1e6]
        'bowlDegree', bowlDegree, 'minCellHits', minCellHits, ... %[output:39d7db33] %[output:5f69987c] %[output:8febe17d] %[output:379ba1e6]
        'refineTOffset', true, 'verbose', false); %[output:39d7db33] %[output:5f69987c] %[output:8febe17d] %[output:379ba1e6]
    hitsIt = rhitApplyCalibration(hits, calibIt); %[output:1f5f897d] %[output:4ba9732c] %[output:30cf1e01] %[output:8ae580ac]

    hM = histcounts(hitsIt.mc, edgesM);
    [pkM, ipM] = max(hM); halfM = pkM / 2;
    LM = find(hM(1:ipM) < halfM, 1, 'last');
    RM = ipM + find(hM(ipM:end) < halfM, 1, 'first') - 1;
    mrpIt = NaN;
    if pkM > 20 && ~isempty(LM) && ~isempty(RM)
        mrpIt = centresM(ipM) / max(centresM(RM) - centresM(LM), eps);
    end
    mrpHistory(it + 1) = mrpIt;
    gain = (mrpIt - mrpHistory(it)) / max(mrpHistory(it), 1);
    fprintf('Iter %d:           M/dM = %.1f  (gain %+.2f%%)\n', it, mrpIt, 100*gain); %[output:11b14b36] %[output:034a3f3c] %[output:02a15ab7] %[output:6000f7e0]
    if mrpIt > mrpHistory(it)
        bestHits = hitsIt; bestCalib = calibIt;
        hits = hitsIt; calib = calibIt; diag = diagIt;
    end
    if abs(gain) < tolerance
        nNoGain = nNoGain + 1;
        if nNoGain >= 2, fprintf('Converged.\n'); break; end
    else
        nNoGain = 0;
    end
end %[output:group:84e2e903]
hits = bestHits; calib = bestCalib;

figure('Color', 'w'); plot(0:numel(mrpHistory(~isnan(mrpHistory)))-1, ... %[output:9725ca51]
    mrpHistory(~isnan(mrpHistory)), 'o-', 'LineWidth', 1.5); %[output:9725ca51]
xlabel('iteration'); ylabel('M / \DeltaM at chosen peak'); grid on; %[output:9725ca51]
title('Iterative refinement: mass-resolving power vs iteration'); %[output:9725ca51]
  %[control:button:0a08]{"position":[1,2]}
%%
%[text] ## 9. Visualise the fitted bowl
%[text] $\\Delta C / C\_0$ across the detector. Real LEAP bowls are asymmetric (not radially symmetric) --- typically a horseshoe pattern with a few-percent excursion.
xs = linspace(-18, 18, 121);
[X, Y] = meshgrid(xs, xs);
Cv  = rhitEvaluateBowl(calib.bowl, X, Y);
dev = 100 * (Cv ./ calib.bowl.coeffs(1) - 1);

figure('Color', 'w'); %[output:5584df80]
imagesc(xs, xs, dev, [-3 3]); %[output:5584df80]
axis image; colorbar; set(gca, 'YDir', 'normal'); %[output:5584df80]
xlabel('detector x (mm)'); ylabel('detector y (mm)'); %[output:5584df80]
title(sprintf('Fitted bowl  \\DeltaC/C_0 (%%);  residual %.4f%%', ... %[output:group:20fb7c7c] %[output:5584df80]
    calib.fitResidualPctC0)); %[output:group:20fb7c7c] %[output:5584df80]
  %[control:button:0a09]{"position":[1,2]}
%%
%[text] ## 10. Build the output *pos* table
%[text] The workflow output is a pos-format table compatible with the rest of the Atom Probe Toolbox (consumable by *posLoad*, *massSpecPlot*, *posAllocateRange*, etc.). The 3D positions *x*, *y*, *z* are set to zero --- this workflow only calibrates mass-to-charge, not 3D reconstruction. Run the IVAS-style reconstruction step separately to populate them.
nIons = height(hits);
pos = table( ...
    (1:nIons)', ...                 % ionIdx
    zeros(nIons, 1), ...            % x  (3D recon not done)
    zeros(nIons, 1), ...            % y
    zeros(nIons, 1), ...            % z
    double(hits.mc), ...            % mc  (calibrated)
    double(hits.tof), ...           % tof (raw, ns)
    double(hits.VDC), ...           % VDC (V)
    double(hits.detx), ...          % detx (mm)
    double(hits.dety), ...          % dety (mm)
    'VariableNames', {'ionIdx','x','y','z','mc','tof','VDC','detx','dety'});
pos.Properties.VariableUnits = ...
    {'1','nm','nm','nm','Da','ns','V','mm','mm'};
pos.Properties.UserData = struct('calibration', calib, ...
    'sourceRhit', meta.fileName, ...
    'note', '3D coordinates (x, y, z) are zero - reconstruction not performed in this workflow');

disp(head(pos)); %[output:1751539c]
fprintf('Output pos table: %d rows, mc range [%.3f, %.3f] Da\n', ... %[output:group:5c0aa015] %[output:89339a9e]
    height(pos), min(pos.mc), max(pos.mc)); %[output:group:5c0aa015] %[output:89339a9e]
  %[control:button:0a10]{"position":[1,2]}
%%
%[text] ## 11. Save calibration and pos table
%[text] *uiputfile* opens a *Save As* dialog. By default both files are written next to the RHIT: `<run>_calib.mat` (calibration struct + Z-range, fiducial, peak list, M/ΔM history as audit trail) and `<run>_calibrated.pos` (the pos table for downstream toolbox use).
calib.zSelection.vdcMin    = vdcMin;
calib.zSelection.vdcMax    = vdcMax;
calib.fiducial.center      = roiDet.Center;
calib.fiducial.semiAxes    = roiDet.SemiAxes;
calib.fiducial.rotation    = roiDet.RotationAngle;
calib.peaksDetected        = peakTable;
calib.mrpHistory           = mrpHistory(~isnan(mrpHistory));

[rPath, rBase] = fileparts(meta.fileName);

% Calibration struct -> .mat
[fName, fPath] = uiputfile({'*.mat', 'MAT files (*.mat)'}, ...
    'Save calibration struct as', fullfile(rPath, [rBase '_calib.mat']));
if ~isequal(fName, 0) %[output:group:37acf986]
    save(fullfile(fPath, fName), '-struct', 'calib');
    fprintf('Saved calibration: %s\n', fullfile(fPath, fName)); %[output:1008f825]
end %[output:group:37acf986]

% Pos table -> .pos (or .mat if .pos export not available)
[fName2, fPath2] = uiputfile({'*.pos', 'pos file (*.pos)'; '*.mat', 'MAT files (*.mat)'}, ...
    'Save calibrated pos table as', fullfile(rPath, [rBase '_calibrated.pos']));
if ~isequal(fName2, 0) %[output:group:06ab65e9]
    out = fullfile(fPath2, fName2);
    if endsWith(out, '.pos', 'IgnoreCase', true) && exist('posExport', 'file')
        posExport(pos, out);
    else
        save(out, 'pos');
    end
    fprintf('Saved pos table:   %s\n', out); %[output:2f0dea09]
end %[output:group:06ab65e9]
