%%
%[text] ## 12. Mapping to Cameca's IVAS terminology  (reference only)
%[text] -  Cameca:   $\\mathrm{Mass} = k \\cdot (T - dT\_0)^2$ with $T = a\_0 / \\sqrt{a\_1 + V\_{DC} + a\_2 V\_{DC}^2}$.
%[text] -  Ours:     $\\mathrm{mc} = C(x, y) \\cdot V\_{DC} \\cdot (t\_{ToF} - t\_{\\mathrm{offset}})^2$. \
%[text] 
%[text] **Step mapping**
%[text] -  *Z-selection rectangle on V(z)* $\\leftrightarrow$ IVAS *Voltage History* ROI.
%[text] -  *Detector ellipse* $\\leftrightarrow$ IVAS *Fiducial*.
%[text] -  *Iteration on M/ΔM* $\\leftrightarrow$ IVAS *Voltage ↔ Bowl* loop until *Auto Stop* condition (default $\\Delta$ resolution = 5).
%[text] -  *t\_offset* $\\leftrightarrow$ $dT\_0$. *C(x, y) · VDC* $\\leftrightarrow$ $k / (a\_1 + V\_{DC} + a\_2 V\_{DC}^2)$ (we set $a\_2 = 0$).
%[text] -  Cameca's bowl is "radial + 96 angular sectors". Our 2D *xy* polynomial of degree 4 (15 terms) is a different basis but captures the same asymmetric shape. \
%%
